    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1293">

                <pb facs="1249" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2637a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-13T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3087. Reports concerning the suffering and increased death rate among German
                    babies owing to milk shortage continue to arouse much sympathy in the United
                    States. Is there any objection to making public Doctor Taylor’s report of April
                    17 transmitted in Embassy’s 2946 of April 18?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
